Package: hsed
Version: 1.0.0
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.34), python3 (>= 3.9)
Recommends: strace
Maintainer: Hidden Space Explorer Maintainers <noreply@localhost>
Description: TUI explorer for disk space hidden in unlinked-but-open files
 Finds files that were deleted (unlinked) but are still held open by a
 process fd - the reason `df -h` can show a full disk while `du -sh` finds
 nothing to account for it. Ships two commands:
 .
  hsed  - the interactive TUI (Textual-based), talks to hsedd over a
          Unix socket. Table view, a reconstructed "hidden filesystem"
          tree, and per-file actions: truncate and reclaim space, send
          SIGHUP for a graceful log reopen, SIGKILL an unresponsive
          process, or live-stream exactly what it is writing right now
          via ptrace.
  hsedd - the privileged backend daemon (systemd unit: hsed.service).
          Does all the actual /proc scanning, ftruncate, signal delivery,
          and ptrace work; hsed is purely a client of its Unix socket
          protocol.
 .
 Live streaming (STREAM) is x86_64-only in this release and requires
 root or CAP_SYS_PTRACE, same as strace/gdb -p.
